<title>FRANCE: Total head sees $16 oil price when Iraq returns.</title>
<headline>Total head sees $16 oil price when Iraq returns.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of French oil group Total SA told l'Agefi newspaper in an interview that he expected a medium-term oil price of $16 per barrel -- against a market price of some $24 now.</p>
<p>&quot;I think that the moment Iraq comes back to the market prices will ease very rapidly,&quot; Thierry Desmarest said.</p>
<p>&quot;On top of that, we forecast for 1997 an increase in production outside the OPEC area which alone will be enough to satisfy the increase in demand,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>&quot;That is why we maintain our medium-term forecasts on the basis of an average of $16 per barrel.&quot;</p>
</text>
